  "description": "R8 P0-5: decisive control for the GARD alignment-artifact verdict. GARD (Faster mode, codon, rc=4 and rc=2) rerun on codon-aware clean realignments (protein MAFFT + back-translation + >50%-gap column filter) of the SAME input sequences used in the original nucleotide-alignment GARD screening. Layered interpretation: (1) the OLD breakpoint positions and pathological partition trees were alignment artifacts (positions shift or trees become healthy after realignment); (2) breakpoints did NOT universally vanish - a residual subset persists at the same sites with healthy trees and strong delta-cAIC, so recombination confounding cannot be claimed excluded for that subset; (3) the screened 50 genes are all classification_v7=gene-driven because they were selected as top-LRT BUSTED hits, so the residual-recombination scope falls entirely within gene-driven claims.",
